---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import FamilyPlan from "../../components/family/FamilyPlan.astro";
---
<Layout title="Family pricing — TinyKite" description="One household subscription for Nesta, Gloss and future TinyKite apps. Free during beta. Planned £4.99/month or £49/year after beta.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground">TinyKite for families</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-text sm:text-5xl">One family. One price.</h1>
    <p class="mb-9 mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-text">Read, learn and stay close. Your household gets Nesta, Gloss and the TinyKite apps we launch next, with one subscription.</p>
    <FamilyPlan />
    <section class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-text" aria-label="Pricing questions">
      <div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Is beta a free trial that starts charging?</h2><p class="mt-2">No. Beta is free, with no payment details required. A grown-up must choose a paid subscription when it becomes available.</p></div>
      <div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Do I pay separately for each app or child?</h2><p class="mt-2">No. The planned price covers your household across Nesta, Gloss and future TinyKite apps. Each app still has its own sharing and child-consent settings.</p></div>
      <div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What does campaign backing pay for?</h2><p class="mt-2">It helps build the shared picture dictionary, with languages added as funding and review capacity allow. Some backer rewards include a year of this same household plan after beta; no separate Gloss subscription. <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/gloss/back/">Explore the Gloss campaign</a>.</p></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
